;; Regulatory source register for the JPN-MOE green-procurement compliance
;; service: the two statutes the actor implements against -- グリーン購入法
;; (Green Purchasing Law) and 環境配慮契約法 (Eco-Contracts Law) -- plus the
;; Act that constitutes the ministry, and the ministry pages that publish
;; both schemes' basic policies.
;;
;; README.md and blueprint.edn ground the actor in env.go.jp sources only.
;; Until this file existed there was no such list, so no claim in this
;; repository could be traced to anything. This is that list.
;;
;; Shape is tx-data (a vector of entity maps), like every other EDN corpus in
;; this workspace, so it loads with
;;   (d/transact conn (edn/read-string (slurp "facts.edn")))
;; :source/id is the join key. A law or page not in this table has NO
;; spec-basis for this repository -- extend the table, never invent an id or
;; a URL.
;;
;; VERIFIED BY `nbb scripts/verify-facts.cljk`, which re-fetches every entry.
;; Each carries a :source/verify tag naming WHICH check establishes it:
;;
;;   :e-gov-law-id   Resolve the law id through the e-Gov law API and require
;;                   the title and the law number to still match. HTTP status
;;                   is never consulted here and must not be: laws.e-gov.go.jp
;;                   answers HTTP 200 for /law/<anything>, rendering "not
;;                   found" client-side, so the /law/ URL cannot tell a real
;;                   citation from an invented one. This register's own first
;;                   draft proved the point: three plausible ids built from
;;                   the year+number convention (412AC0000000100 et al.)
;;                   returned total_count 0 through the API while their /law/
;;                   URLs would have loaded -- the ids e-Gov actually holds
;;                   carry an extra revision digit the convention does not
;;                   predict.
;;
;;   :page-identity  Fetch and require four things together: a 2xx, a final
;;                   URL that is still the page asked for, the declared
;;                   charset, and the <title> recorded below.
;;
;;   :page-text      All of :page-identity, plus every string in
;;                   :page/must-contain present in the de-tagged body.
;;
;; HOST ASSUMPTIONS ARE MEASURED AT RUN TIME, NOT DATED IN A COMMENT.
;; The :host-behaviour entities below say what each host does with a path
;; that does not exist, and the verifier re-fetches one on every run.
;;
;; MEASURED 2026-08-31: www.env.go.jp answers HTTP 404 -- not the 403 the
;; sibling METI register measures on all four of its hosts -- with a real
;; 45364-byte お探しのページは見つかりません page at the requested URL,
;; whose title differs from the ministry home title, so status and title
;; both separate a real page from an invented one. No bot challenge was seen
;; on either host here across the probes that built this register. That is a
;; measurement of this run, not a property: the entity below pins the status
;; and the run re-measures it.
;;
;; THE SECOND HOST IS A MOE-AFFILIATED BODY, NOT ANOTHER BUREAU OF THE
;; MINISTRY. 環境省 has no extra-ministerial bureaux on their own hosts --
;; unlike METI's 特許庁/中小企業庁/資源エネルギー庁 -- and the verifier
;; refuses a register whose :page-identity entries all sit on one host,
;; because the four page self-tests aimed at a single host are exactly the
;; burst that trips a bot challenge. The second host cited here is
;; www.nies.go.jp, 国立環境研究所 -- the national research institute this
;; ministry supervises. It is a public procurement entity itself, and one of
;; the 国等 the Eco-Contracts Law addresses. Its home page is cited at
;; identity level only.
;;
;; :source/covers says why an entry is in a green-procurement register.
;; Claims stop at the level actually checked -- law identity, and for the
;; pages the title, the URL, the charset and the strings read on
;; 2026-08-31. No article text and no PDF is asserted, because none was
;; read.

[
 ;; ── What each host does with a path that does not exist ────────────────────
 ;; Re-measured on every run.

 {:source/id "host.www-env-go-jp"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "www.env.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 404
  :source/note "環境省 itself. A nonexistent path answers HTTP 404 -- NOT the
                403 all four METI-family hosts measure -- with a 45364-byte
                お探しのページは見つかりません page served at the requested
                URL, titled お探しのページは見つかりません | 環境省, which
                differs from the home title 環境省へようこそ！, so both status
                and title separate a real page from a soft 404. Measured
                2026-08-31 with no bot challenge in front of it; the run
                re-measures rather than trusting this note."}

 {:source/id "host.www-nies-go-jp"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "www.nies.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 404
  :source/note "国立環境研究所. A nonexistent path answers HTTP 404 with a
                24217-byte page titled 404 Not Found｜トップ｜国立環境研究所
                -- a different title and byte count from the ministry host's
                not-found page, on a different host. Only a real 2xx page
                body for a path that does not exist is a failure here."}

